.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
.TH OCTA-PRESET 1 "" "OCTA-CAPTURE @PROJECT_VERSION@" "OCTA-CAPTURE Manual"
.SH NAME
octa\-preset \- inspect, save, apply or recover OCTA-CAPTURE settings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBocta-preset inspect|normalize\fR FILE
\fBocta-preset export\fR [CTRL-PORT] > settings.octa
\fBocta-preset prepare\fR FILE CURRENT.syx > prepared.syx
\fBocta-preset apply\fR FILE NEW-RECOVERY.syx [CTRL-PORT]
\fBocta-preset restore|restore-auto\fR RECOVERY.syx [CTRL-PORT]
\fBocta-preset memory-store|memory-load\fR NEW-RECOVERY.syx [CTRL-PORT]
\fBocta-preset routing\fR multi-monitor|playback NEW-RECOVERY.syx [CTRL-PORT]
\fBocta-preset direct-out\fR NEW-RECOVERY.syx [CTRL-PORT]
\fBocta-preset initialize\fR all|preamps|direct-mix|reverb|patchbay NEW-RECOVERY.syx [CTRL-PORT]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspect, normalize and prepare operate on local files without hardware.
Normalize and export write binary Ver100 .octa data to standard output.
Export reads current hardware state. Prepare combines an imported preset with
a supplied current raw snapshot and writes the prepared SysEx frame.
.PP
Apply, initialization, routing, Direct Out and device-memory commands change hardware.
They create a new raw recovery file before writes and verify fresh state afterward.
Keep recovery files after errors. Restore writes a saved raw snapshot;
restore-auto uses the Auto-Sens recovery path.
.PP
Memory-store overwrites persistent device memory. A runtime snapshot cannot undo
a previous persistent-memory preset after it has been overwritten.
Initialization can change input power settings; choose the target deliberately.
.PP
The default CTRL MIDI port is hw:CARD=OCTACAPTURE,DEV=0,SUBDEV=1. Close other control-panel/CTRL clients before opening it. Audio streaming is independent of this connection.

.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success; nonzero indicates a usage, device or operation error.
.SH SEE ALSO
octa-capture(1), octa-status(1), octa-preset(1)
